{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Bullish Spikes: The model consistently fails to capture the magnitude of upward price surges (e.g., the rise from ~76 to ~89 in late November), forecasting a flat or slightly upward trend while actual prices jump significantly. Apply a positive bias correction of +10 to +15 EUR when the 3-day price momentum exceeds 5%.",
    "Severe Lag in Trend Reversal: Forecasts exhibit a delayed reaction to trend changes, often continuing to project the previous day's price or a slow drift rather than the immediate volatility seen in the true outcome. Implement a lag-correction factor that accelerates the forecast slope by 2x during the first 5 days of a new trend.",
    "Overshoot Correction Post-Spike: After a major price spike (e.g., hitting 89 EUR), the model's mean-reversion logic is too slow, predicting a gradual decline while the actual market corrects more sharply or stabilizes at a higher floor. Reduce the forecast slope by 30% immediately following a 3-day cumulative gain >10% to account for faster mean reversion.",
    "Sentiment Ignorance: The model ignores positive sentiment signals (values > 0.20) in the history, treating them as noise. When sentiment history contains values >= 0.25, increase the base forecast by 3-5 EUR and extend the bullish trajectory by 3 additional days.",
    "Horizon-Specific Drift: The 30-day forecast shows a linear drift that diverges increasingly from reality over time. Replace the linear extrapolation with a mean-reverting curve anchored to the 20-day moving average of the true outcome to prevent cumulative error growth."
  ]
}
